  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Israr vs State Of Uttarakhand & Others on 24 March, 2015 Author: U. C. Dhyani Bench: U. C. Dhyani Wpcrl No.326 of 2015 Hon'ble U. C. Dhyani, J. Mr. S. K. Shandilya, Advocate present for the petitioner.",
    "facts": "By means of present criminal writ petition, the petitioner seeks to issue a writ, order or direction in the nature of certiorari quashing the impugned order dated 10.12.2014 passed by respondent no.2- Adjudicating Officer, Haridwar in case no.6 of 2014 under Section 51 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "The principal submission of learned counsel for the petitioner is that the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal has not been constituted in the State as yet and therefore, the petitioner cannot challenge the impugned order of the adjudicating Officer before the said Tribunal.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "The principal submission of learned counsel for the petitioner is that the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal has not been constituted in the State as yet and therefore, the petitioner cannot challenge the impugned order of the adjudicating Officer before the said Tribunal.",
